.rule-coverage.json
# Without the trailing slash. A pattern ending in one matches a directory
# and nothing else, and on the machines that build this cache the path is
# a symbolic link -- so the name went on being offered for commit there,
# twice. The specification is not redistributable; what sits here never
# belongs in the history, whichever shape the path takes.
.spec-cache
docs/consortium/
docs/private/

